<title>MEXICO: Mexico Jan-Feb steel production up 5.4 pct - ass'n.</title>
<headline>Mexico Jan-Feb steel production up 5.4 pct - ass'n.</headline>
<dateline>MONTERREY, Mexico 1997-05-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Mexico's total liquid steel output rose 5.4 percent in the first two months of the year compared with 1996, the National Steel and Iron industry said.</p>
<p>Output rose to 2.268 million tonnes for the months, and was 1.11 million in February, the chamber said in an internal document obtained by Reuters.</p>
<p>In the time period, rolled product output rose 5.4 percent to 828,228 tonnes, &quot;thanks to the good performance of flat products and seamless pipes, which rose 11.3 and 14 percent, respectively,&quot; the chamber report said.</p>
<p>The chamber outlined output for the first two months in metric tonnes:</p>
<p>   Type		   Jan-Feb '97     Jan-Feb '96   Pct chng</p>
<p>Mini-mill		   1,445,219	 1,380,146	 4.7</p>
<p>Blast furnace		 822,789	   771,999	 6.6</p>
<p>Total liquid steel	2,268,008	 2,152,145	 5.4</p>
<p>Semi-finished		 392,333	   365,136	 7.4</p>
<p>Total rolled products   1,694,673	 1,608,492	 5.4</p>
<p>Total flat products	 828,228	   744,038	11.3</p>
<p>   Slab			 124,068	    99,506	24.7</p>
<p>   Hot rolled sheet	 384,434	   382,200	 0.6</p>
<p>   Cold rolled sheet	319,726	   262,562	21.8</p>
<p>Total non-flat		763,075	   773,767	-1.4</p>
<p>   Wire rod		   212,487	   205,522	 3.4</p>
<p>   Corrugated bar	   396,447	   414,468	-4.3</p>
<p>   Commercial shapes	 42,279	    42,936	-1.5</p>
<p>   Structural size shapes  55,566	    60,503	-8.2</p>
<p>   Bars			  56,296	    50,308	11.9</p>
<p>   Seamless pipe	    103,370	    90,637	14.0</p>
<p>((--Daniel Perez-Whitaker, Monterrey bureau +528 3457617))</p>
</text>
